			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839570">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> Tale</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Bittersweet Political Thriller (if that's a thing)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Short story fragments, switching characters to spotlight the greater plot unfolding from different perspectives.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Completely outnumbered and doubfounded by the Foundation going all-out during <a href="/scp-5000">SCP-5000</a>, the Insurgency tries to get the ☽☽☽-Initative to intervene.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The cunning, but also very bold gambit of the CI to get the ☽☽☽-Initative into fighting the &quot;Why?&quot;-Foundation (which obviously fails), from them acquiring their first intel on Corbenic up to a forced &quot;audience&quot; infront of the Central Cabal, putting them into massive zugzwang. A somewhat different take on the fable of the mouse getting the bear to fight the fox.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Acting as misguided heroes/anti-villains and faced with an enemy they can't use brute force on, I want to emphazise all the other, non-violent subversive means by which they can coerce those mightier than them.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> If this idea seems crazy, that might be exactly it's appeal. Also, if this is any help, i'm not a greenhorn, I just prefered posting on my native branch and now try to get a foothold on the mainsite.</p>

