				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zesc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5703022); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5703022&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607843267" alt="Zesc" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5703022)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zesc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5703022); return false;" >Zesc</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607809500 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">12 Dec 2020 21:45</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843255">
									

<p>Sure thing, I was craving for answering this (but couldn't before due to space constraints).</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Collapsible&nbsp;so&nbsp;Zyn&nbsp;doesn't&nbsp;come&nbsp;suplexing&nbsp;me&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;name&nbsp;of&nbsp;mobile&nbsp;users</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Anyway, for the characters, I have (besides the established folks from the ☽☽☽-Initative) nobody who really &quot;stands out&quot; - in fact, the first two folks are literally nameless mooks referred to by their job. Given that I'm constantly perspective swapping, wasting time on fleshing out the on-offs too much would harm the narrative, imho.</p>
<p>The first &quot;scene&quot; covers how the Insurgency acquired knowledge of Corbenic (or atleast the tech to communicate there), in what is essentially &quot;reframing Dr. Spiegels death in a car crash as assassination ploy&quot; (hopefully <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/daveyoufool" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2034230); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2034230&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607810465" alt="daveyoufool" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2034230)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/daveyoufool" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2034230); return false;">daveyoufool</a></span> will be okay with that).</p>
<p>After that I want to jump directly into the 5000-Action, with the Insurgency being decimated before they even can react and a last, lethaly wound insurgent using his last moments to send out a &quot;message in a bottle&quot; - I'm a huge fan of &quot;contigency plans withing contigency plans&quot;, and this is pretty much where the gears start turning.</p>
<p>The rest of the story plays within Corbenic during the plot of Why? unfolding (e.g. 2020-01-02 to 2020-04-12<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-192934-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-192934-1')">1</a></sup>).</p>
<p>Knowing that the Initiative could crush them with ease, the Insurgency resorts to multiple nonviolent resistance methods to face them.</p>
<p>This includes simple civil disobediance against the Initiative (just imagine the distrust a single charismatic leader can spark amongst the huge influx of new-quietus<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-192934-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-192934-2')">2</a></sup>) up to full blown agitprop campaigns against the Initiative. (Afterall, they have <a href="/scp-4839">intervened in the past</a> - what justification do they have to ignore this event?)</p>
<p>Eventually, a great mass of Insurgents will just peacefully turn themselves in to the authorities - not the new-quietus though, but older Insurgents, some of them former double-agents that undercut the Initiative. This does not just causes chaos, but is also their ultimate threat: they have given up their covers themselves; nobody knows how many of them are still amidst them.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-192934-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-192934-3')">3</a></sup></p>
<p>All together, they can even pressure the Initiative in hearing them in an attempt to buy time whilst trying to figure out who coordinates<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-192934-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-192934-4')">4</a></sup> the Insurgency, and stopping them.</p>
<p>In the end&#8230; their efforts were in vain, probably. Because as we all know, project PNEUMA never happened and they got nowhere before it &quot;un-happened&quot;. I don't want to ruin the really good ending of SCP-5000, so trying to keep the ambigous ending both bittersweet but also deeply disturbing (from the perspective of the afterlife) might be in need for critique the most later on.</p>
